Subject: [PATCH] Key seed images by the selected wheel's content

Downstream wheel backports can change contents without changing the wheel
filename. Include the selected wheel's SHA-256 in the installation-image
key so successive same-version replacements build separate images while
byte-identical wheels continue to reuse their images.

Keep the existing installer/Python separation and locking. Leave legacy
images and images used by existing environments untouched. No date or RPM
release needs to be maintained in the cache key.

Cover copy and symlink seeding with both embedded pip versions, migration
from filename-only images, repeated replacements with unchanged size and
mtime, reuse across locations and rollback, and unreadable-wheel errors.

Related Azure Linux PR: 19710
Upstream-status: Pending

